# UniMap latest sorting settings

Read only. Do not click Edit, Print Chute Label, Add New Sorting Plan, switch presets, or change any field except the search filters below.

1. Log in at https://dispatch.uniuni.com/login with `UNIUNI_USERNAME` and `UNIUNI_PASSWORD` from `.env`. Dismiss a What's New dialog only if it blocks the menu.
2. On https://dispatch.uniuni.com/main, Menu → SORTING MACHINE CONFIGURATION (NEW).
3. Leave Sorting Machine selected. Set Sorting Center = NJ Warehouse, Sorting Method = 9, Sorting Mode = Sort by routes. Click Search.
4. The plan marked Active is the live setting. Read the whole chute table, including rows below the fold. Columns: COMPT, Bundle Type, Dest./Transit WHS, Assigned Routes / Zones.

Compare that table to `chute_destination_gofo`. A row applies on an ops day when `effective_date` is null or on/before that day, and `end_date` is null or on/after that day. Unchanged chutes keep `end_date` null. A changed chute's old rows keep their `effective_date` and get an `end_date`. If that chute has no newer `effective_date`, it has ended. If it has a newer `effective_date`, the latest open row is current.

An evening start belongs to the next calendar ops day. The 6:10pm scrape on 2026-10-22 is still ops day 2026-10-22. The 6:30pm scrape that evening opens ops day 2026-10-23 and reads the new Batch No. The 1021-gofo plan is already loaded for ops day 2026-10-23: changed chutes end on 2026-10-22, and their new rows start on 2026-10-23. Chutes 420 and 620 keep ORD184 uni_hub and add their new routes in that same batch: 420 adds the ORD02 routes, 620 adds 125385.33-IND.H-LEX01-010-H. Chutes 417, 418, 617, and 1069 ended on 2026-10-22 and have no successor. Chutes 267, 860, 914, 915, and 916 start again on 2026-10-23. Chute 515 stays EWR.H by_route. Chute 567 on 2026-10-23 is JFK175 by_city with FRG01 60-U through 66-U, 68-U, and 69-U; 60-U is 185186.22. The 18:21 ET edit on 2026-10-25 opens ops day 2026-10-26: chute 320 is JFK175 by_city with 185187.22-EWR.H-FRG01-62-U and 185194.22-EWR.H-FRG01-69-U. Chute 367 stays JFK175 by_city and adds 185011.21-JFK.H-JFK01-32-U and 185018.21-JFK.H-JFK01-39-U to the 10/23 routes. Chute 567 stays JFK175 by_city, drops 62-U and 69-U, and 60-U is 185185.22 again while 61-U is 185186.22. Chutes 470, 518, and 1020 stay ORD184, DFW445, and MIA307 uni_hub; a route-only change on a uni_hub chute is not stored. Chute 866 has no setting on 2026-10-23. Chute 315 has no setting on 2026-10-23. Chute 514 starts 2026-10-23 as EWR.H by_route with 185192.22-EWR.H-FRG01-67-G.

Mid-day switch on ops day 2026-10-29: scrapes before 12:10 ET still use the prior plan; scrapes at or after 12:10 ET stay on ops day 2026-10-29 but use plan `458隔口配置`. Mark the prior open rows with `end_date = 2026-10-29`. New rows from `458隔口配置` start `effective_date = 2026-10-29`. That plan adds 5-digit and 6-digit chute ids (for example 10101 beside 101, 106401 beside 1064): treat them as new chute ids with their own routes, not as aliases of the 3-digit physical slot. Read `458隔口配置` for the full live table after 12:10, including unchanged 3-digit chutes. Chute 669 is JFK175 by_route with 185191.22-EWR.H-FRG01-66-U (not EWR.H). Do not insert another copy unless the user reports a newer live change.

5/6-digit split volumes are not on the heat map. On Sorting Production Analysis they appear in the **Irregular chutes** table (Chute / Parcels = cumulative batch volume at query time). The scraper stores those rows in `chute_volume` alongside the 400-grid; Pull includes them when volume is 1–199 and the chute is configured.

